  "prefLabel": "Lab 1402.13 Engulfment",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Lab 1402.13 “Engulfment” means the surrounding and effective capture of a person by a liquid or finely divided or flowable solid substance that can be aspirated to cause death by filling or plugging the respiratory system or that can exert enough force on the body to cause death by strangulation, constriction, or crushing.\n\nSource. #14431, eff 11-22-25, EXPIRES: 11-22-35",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/lab1400.html"
